    "faq": {
      "type": "faq-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do waterproof socks actually work?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. There’s a waterproof layer sealed inside the sock, so rain, puddles and wet ground don’t reach your foot. Two things worth knowing: water that comes in over the top of the sock stays in, and if you work hard you’ll still sweat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will my feet get sweaty?",
            "answer": "<p>Less than you’d expect, but yes if you push hard. The middle layer lets sweat out as vapour, which buys you a lot of time. Walking, work and commuting are comfortably within it. A hard run in mild weather isn’t.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do they replace waterproof boots?",
            "answer": "<p>No. They’re the layer that keeps working after your boots have soaked through, which on a wet day is usually a matter of when rather than if. They don’t give you grip or ankle support.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_wudu": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use them for wudu?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, that’s what a lot of people buy them for. They’re waterproof, they hold their shape and they stay on your foot. Two UK scholars have examined them, and the wudu page explains it properly.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What size do I get?",
            "answer": "<p>Four sizes cover UK 3 to 14. S is 3–5, M is 6–8, L is 9–11, XL is 12–14. If you’re between two, take the bigger one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much is delivery?",
            "answer": "<p>Free on two pairs or more. On a single pair there’s a delivery charge, and you’ll see the full total before anything goes in your basket.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why are there no reviews?",
            "answer": "<p>Because we don’t have any yet. We’re new, and a few five-star reviews with nothing behind them aren’t worth reading. When there are real ones they’ll go here, including the bad ones.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who am I buying from?",
            "answer": "<p>HydroSox, a UK company at 399–405 Oxford Street, Mayfair, London W1C 2BU. Our phone number and email are at the bottom of every page.</p>"
          }
        }
